+## Phase 3 — static coverage (FIRST PASS DONE 2026-10-09)
+
+Tooling lives in the title repo (`prepare_images.py`, `capture_session.py`,
+`gen_banks.py`) on top of the framework's `ingest_coverage_manifests.py`.
+
+What was measured (macOS arm64, FreeBIOS direct boot, headless):
+
+- One short session (title, left-handed prompt, ~1,500 VBlanks) produced a
+  manifest with 101 captured code pages. 92 resolved to ROM content with no
+  dumped bytes: the ARM7 module runs from **two relocated aliases**
+  (`0x037F7E18`, `0x027D0968`), the ARM9 image from `0x02000000`, and overlays
+  000 and 045 from slots `0x0227CB20` / `0x02287660`. 9 pages are
+  runtime-materialised (ITCM page, ARM7 pages at `0x027F7000`/`0x03807000`,
+  overlay-band pages) and became captured-page banks.
+- 15 content-validated banks (coverage-driven) and 178 (with
+  `--all-overlays`: every ROM overlay emitted at its table address).
+- **Differential vs the all-interpreted run, same script:** frame hashes of
+  both screens identical at 300/600/700/900/1500 VBlanks; `insn9`/`insn7`
+  identical (261,799,174 / 37,389,093 at 1,500). Tier-3 instructions:
+  ARM9 261.7M -> **0**, ARM7 36.0M -> **8** (2 entries, unidentified).
+- No `dispatch_misses.log` produced.
+
+Caveats: this is in-sample (the banks were seeded from the same flow); a
+minigame path will exercise overlays whose seeds are entry-only until they are
+captured. Reaching minigames needs input that advances past the title (taps on
+the "Touch me!" character did not advance it; the left-handed prompt does
+respond to touch, so the touch path itself works). The `--all-overlays` runner
+binary is ~100 MB; split/trim before packaging.
+
+Next in this phase: advance past the title (find the right input), capture
+per-minigame manifests, rerun ingest (monotonic), regenerate, and repeat the
+differential. Close the 2 ARM7 entries. Re-seed with `--owned-rows-*` so seeds
+are the honest remainder.
 
